    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0183" n="165" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg165"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.333D3/9–546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pawley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-05T19:00:00-04:00">September 5, 1946—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1190. After agreeing to cooperate fully in world coffee study now being
                    undertaken by Inter-Amer Coffee Board (1) through furnishing of basic coffee
                    data requested by Board directly from DNC and (2) providing services of Braz
                    expert in actual preparation of study here, Brazil has failed to carry out this
                    cooperation in either respect. Without Braz assistance, particularly in
                    furnishing of basic data, coffee study either cannot be completed at all or if
                    completed will <pb facs="0184" n="166" xml:id="pg166"/> lack authority which it
                    is intended to have. Main reason US favors extension Inter-Amer Coffee Agreement
                    for 1 year is completion this study.</p>
                <p>Please impress this situation on appropriate authorities and ascertain (1)
                    whether Brazil intends to sign protocol for 1 year extension Agreement from Oct
                    1 and (2) whether Brazil intends provide necessary cooperation in coffee
                        study.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d132-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clayton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d132-f1" n="9" xml:id="d132-f1-content">
                <p>The inquiry by the Acting Secretary was repeated in telegram 1226, September 17,
                    1946, 4 p.m. (561.333D3/9–546). The agreement was signed by Brazil, along with
                    other countries, and dated as of October 1, 1946. For text, see Department of
                    State Treaties and Other International Acts Series No. 1605.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
